## SQ-DRK-04 | spout fills a bottle from Kiwi Tea (diagnostic: recipe presence)
@group A
@commands Spout and Item Drain: fill a glass bottle from 250 mB of `creativeengineering:kiwi_tea`, `lychee_juice`, `chorus_tea`, `sea_grape_juice` (creative fluid tank); drain a Kiwi Tea back
@pass each fills one bottle of the matching item and drains back to 250 mB
@fails createBottle pair missing for that fluid
@from batches/r1103/p2_R2.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
# r1103 p2: every spout line read "needs -1 mB, gives nothing" (no filling recipe matched) while the drain worked;
# NCH createBottle makes the filling and emptying pair together. List both recipes and retry the spout.
> cdevtest recipes kiwi_tea
> cdevtest recipes lychee_juice
> cdevtest bytype create:filling
> s5 spout creativedelight:kiwi_tea 250 minecraft:glass_bottle
> s5 spout minecraft:water 250 minecraft:glass_bottle
expect \[cdevtest\] verb=bytype id=\S*filling\S*kiwi_tea\S* result=
expect \[s5\] spout creativedelight:kiwi_tea 250 mB into minecraft:glass_bottle: can true, needs 250 mB, gives creativedelight:kiwi_tea x1
look the water spout line is the probe control (vanilla potion fill); if it also reads -1, the probe is wrong, not the pack

